Then the scales, claws, fangs,
and bones of the creature.

6
00:00:19,513 --> 00:00:22,984
They were used to create high
quality weapons and medicine.

7
00:00:23,113 --> 00:00:25,642
It brought great wealth
to the countryside.

8
00:00:25,813 --> 00:00:26,643
Wow.

9
00:00:27,333 --> 00:00:31,073
After that, the brave and
mighty adventurer was a hero,

10
00:00:31,333 --> 00:00:34,013
who the people called the Dragon Slayer.

11
00:00:34,193 --> 00:00:35,233
I want to be one!

12
00:00:35,413 --> 00:00:37,119
I want to be a Dragon Slayer!

13
00:00:37,713 --> 00:00:39,253
That's no easy task.

14
00:00:39,573 --> 00:00:44,110
Some dragons are incredibly tough and fierce,
and have lived for thousands of years.

15
00:00:44,193 --> 00:00:47,233
They can make the ground
tremble just by walking,

16
00:00:47,453 --> 00:00:50,250
and even crumble mountains
with a swat of their tail.

17
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:55,433
In fact, long ago this continent was almost
destroyed by the dragons running wild.

18
00:00:55,953 --> 00:01:02,410
They'd chomp on little kids
like you for a snack huh?

19
00:01:02,493 --> 00:01:09,493
What's

20
00:01:11,293 --> 00:01:12,123
that

21
00:01:12,206 --> 00:01:13,036
over there huh?

22
00:01:13,119 --> 00:01:16,250
Is it trouble I don't know but I
have this crazy feeling something's

23
00:01:16,333 --> 00:01:22,090
out there Ahead of us I don't see

24
00:01:22,173 --> 00:01:25,393
anything you don't it's right there

25
00:01:28,073 --> 00:01:32,193
How can this be a dragon of calamity?

26
00:01:46,633 --> 00:01:53,433
Oh my God.

27
00:02:17,633 --> 00:02:20,813
It's not that you can't return to the end.

28
00:02:22,633 --> 00:02:26,690
It's not that you can't be.

29
00:02:26,773 --> 00:02:28,302
I'll never forget the end.

30
00:02:29,573 --> 00:02:32,330
Let's do it again.

31
00:02:32,413 --> 00:02:34,550
I'm not sure you can't feel it.

32
00:02:34,633 --> 00:02:35,550
I'm not sure you can't feel it.

33
00:02:35,633 --> 00:02:37,339
I'm not sure what's going on.

34
00:02:40,533 --> 00:02:46,613
I'm not sure what's going on?

35
00:03:21,013 --> 00:03:22,533
I don't believe it.

36
00:03:22,893 --> 00:03:26,753
Does the Empire not understand
the terror they have unleashed?

37
00:03:26,893 --> 00:03:28,890
Our records state that it's only been 150

38
00:03:28,973 --> 00:03:31,490
years since the beast
fell into hibernation.

39
00:03:31,573 --> 00:03:34,973
It should be in its dormant
period right now. The fools!

40
00:03:35,353 --> 00:03:36,529
What are they doing?

41
00:03:36,713 --> 00:03:40,713
Who resorts to using something so
devastating over a simple dispute?

42
00:03:54,333 --> 00:03:55,173
Quickly now,

43
00:03:55,453 --> 00:03:57,230
round up everyone who took shelter in the

44
00:03:57,313 --> 00:03:59,842
capital and have them
evacuate immediately.

45
00:04:00,493 --> 00:04:02,033
Everyone! Yes, sir.

46
00:04:02,513 --> 00:04:04,490
If they try to stay, carry them out.

47
00:04:04,573 --> 00:04:07,390
If they cling to their
belongings, drag them away.

48
00:04:07,473 --> 00:04:09,885
Leave not a single person in the capital.

49
00:04:17,393 --> 00:04:20,433
I'm sensing that obstruction
magic is being used.

50
00:04:20,713 --> 00:04:22,133
It's blocking the exits.

51
00:04:23,493 --> 00:04:25,090
It'll be impossible now.

52
00:04:25,173 --> 00:04:27,585
The Sovereign Six won't be able to unite.

53
00:04:37,653 --> 00:04:39,673
Damn these rich nuisances!

54
00:04:48,973 --> 00:04:50,620
Majesty, you must leave now.

55
00:04:50,793 --> 00:04:53,550
When that thing gets here,
we won't stand a chance.

56
00:04:53,633 --> 00:04:56,104
I need you warriors to protect the people.

57
00:04:56,233 --> 00:04:58,450
Focus on guiding them
away from the capital

58
00:04:58,533 --> 00:05:00,945
and take refuge wherever you can find it.

59
00:05:01,233 --> 00:05:04,939
I still have my own responsibilities
right here in the capital.

60
00:05:09,993 --> 00:05:11,653
In the path of that dragon,

61
00:05:12,073 --> 00:05:14,670
there is no doubt the capital
will be thoroughly destroyed.

62
00:05:14,753 --> 00:05:18,133
Right now, they should
be evacuating everyone.

63
00:05:18,933 --> 00:05:19,893
If so, then,

64
00:05:20,353 --> 00:05:24,773
my father, he'll surely choose to stay
behind and use himself as a shield.

65
00:05:25,253 --> 00:05:26,813
But then...

66
00:05:27,613 --> 00:05:28,443
I know.

67
00:05:28,526 --> 00:05:32,593
Even someone as strong as him is
no match for something like that.

68
00:05:35,793 --> 00:05:36,890
Please, father.

69
00:05:36,973 --> 00:05:38,333
You must leave.

70
00:05:40,593 --> 00:05:42,053
A dragon, huh?

71
00:05:43,713 --> 00:05:44,543
Huh?

72
00:05:44,626 --> 00:05:45,530
Wow, they're even bigger than I thought.

73
00:05:45,613 --> 00:05:48,378
This is the first one
I've ever seen in person.

74
00:05:49,113 --> 00:05:49,943
What?

75
00:05:50,026 --> 00:05:50,913
You sure about that?

76
00:05:51,073 --> 00:05:53,544
Uh, he just defeated a Black Death Dragon.

77
00:05:54,373 --> 00:05:55,203
Hey, uh, Lin?

78
00:05:55,286 --> 00:05:59,449
Do you happen to know if your brother
and father are still in the city?

79
00:06:01,073 --> 00:06:01,903
Yes.

80
00:06:01,986 --> 00:06:03,530
I have no doubt they've stayed behind.

81
00:06:03,613 --> 00:06:06,593
But it's too late for us to help them.

82
00:06:06,813 --> 00:06:09,313
No, I think I can do it.

83
00:06:09,573 --> 00:06:10,453
If I run.

84
00:06:12,373 --> 00:06:13,203
Hmm?

85
00:06:13,286 --> 00:06:14,116
If you run?

86
00:06:14,199 --> 00:06:15,653
Look how far away we are.

87
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:17,623
Yeah.

88
00:06:17,706 --> 00:06:19,430
Remember what we did against the goblin?

89
00:06:19,513 --> 00:06:21,278
I think we could do that here.

90
00:06:21,693 --> 00:06:23,893
You mean the wind blast we used?

91
00:06:24,513 --> 00:06:27,193
Yeah, I suppose that would be one option.

92
00:06:27,513 --> 00:06:29,748
But it's going to hit you pretty hard.

93
00:06:30,173 --> 00:06:32,585
Nah, the sword will take the brunt of it.

94
00:06:33,813 --> 00:06:35,013
Let me help out.

95
00:06:35,453 --> 00:06:37,910
I owe a lot to your dad
and the people of the city.

96
00:06:37,993 --> 00:06:40,393
And I want to lend them a hand if I can.

97
00:06:40,893 --> 00:06:43,128
Getting him out shouldn't be too hard.

98
00:06:43,953 --> 00:06:46,247
Surely I can handle that much at least.

99
00:06:48,213 --> 00:06:49,773
Okay, I guess so.

100
00:06:54,013 --> 00:06:55,053
Stop it, Lin.

101
00:06:55,373 --> 00:06:57,726
Why am I sitting here being pessimistic?

102
00:06:57,973 --> 00:07:00,793
He's my teacher, and he
says he can handle it.

103
00:07:01,813 --> 00:07:05,673
Now, Wind Blast is not normally
a spell that's used on people.

104
00:07:06,513 --> 00:07:11,093
But this is one person who I should
not try to compare with anybody normal.

105
00:07:12,153 --> 00:07:13,800
There's no need to hesitate.

106
00:07:15,033 --> 00:07:17,110
That's what you're telling me, right?

107
00:07:17,193 --> 00:07:18,023
Huh?

108
00:07:19,893 --> 00:07:21,933
Foolish of you, King Clays.

109
00:07:22,153 --> 00:07:26,212
Crushing your meager country into
submission is a simple task for me.

110
00:07:26,373 --> 00:07:28,450
No matter the extent of your threats,

111
00:07:28,533 --> 00:07:31,850
I cannot and will not hand the
Dungeon of the Lost over to you.

112
00:07:31,933 --> 00:07:35,753
Your idle hands are letting
such great power go to waste.

113
00:07:36,013 --> 00:07:38,470
Combined with the
intelligence of my empire,

114
00:07:38,553 --> 00:07:42,670
it could be a military force strong
enough to control the known world.

115
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:46,690
We merely chose not to use a power
that's beyond what we can control.

116
00:07:46,773 --> 00:07:50,302
Surely you can understand the
repercussions of such a thing?

117
00:07:50,433 --> 00:07:55,533
And that is precisely why you will
forever be a king of insignificance.

118
00:07:55,713 --> 00:08:00,173
As long as I've known you, you have
never had the starch in you to rule.

119
00:08:10,753 --> 00:08:13,165
There's nothing else that he cares about.

120
00:08:13,333 --> 00:08:16,686
He only wants to get his hands
on what's in that dungeon.

121
00:08:20,093 --> 00:08:21,393
I underestimated him.

122
00:08:21,593 --> 00:08:25,490
I never expected he would throw the
full force of his might like this.

123
00:08:25,573 --> 00:08:29,173
Letting negotiations break
down was a mistake on my part.

124
00:08:53,893 --> 00:08:58,710
The capital faces certain doom and
all I can think about is my daughter,

125
00:08:58,793 --> 00:09:00,173
some leader I am.

126
00:09:02,713 --> 00:09:04,410
Never had it in me to be king.

127
00:09:04,493 --> 00:09:05,770
He's exactly right.

128
00:09:05,853 --> 00:09:07,313
I know who I am.

129
00:09:07,553 --> 00:09:10,435
I've always been more
suited for the battlefield.

130
00:09:11,593 --> 00:09:13,930
I'm truly sorry to the people of this fine

131
00:09:14,013 --> 00:09:17,013
country who have blindly
obeyed their foolish king.

132
00:09:17,613 --> 00:09:21,773
It won't be enough to make amends
for my sins, but at the very least,

133
00:09:21,933 --> 00:09:24,793
I'm going to take one of
its damn eyes with me!

134
00:09:27,373 --> 00:09:28,773
Summon Divine Shield!

135
00:09:33,193 --> 00:09:35,853
Sir Noor, stand in front of this cylinder.

136
00:09:45,533 --> 00:09:46,893
Magic Barrier!

137
00:09:48,453 --> 00:09:49,283
Reflect!

138
00:09:50,033 --> 00:09:51,293
Magic Reflect!

139
00:09:52,173 --> 00:09:53,003
Enhance!

140
00:09:53,086 --> 00:09:54,273
What's that?

141
00:09:54,473 --> 00:09:59,350
Charge Burst It seems different
from the last time we did this?

142
00:09:59,433 --> 00:10:00,273
Condense!

143
00:10:01,033 --> 00:10:02,553
Right, here we go.

144
00:10:03,033 --> 00:10:03,913
The impact.

145
00:10:04,213 --> 00:10:06,684
It'll be much more intense than last time.

146
00:10:06,873 --> 00:10:08,108
Apologies in advance.

147
00:10:08,193 --> 00:10:09,023
What?

148
00:10:09,106 --> 00:10:10,693
Hold on, I... Multi-cast!

149
00:10:12,413 --> 00:10:15,433
Okay, I've put everything
that I have into this.

150
00:10:15,873 --> 00:10:17,133
Six-fold cast!

151
00:10:17,473 --> 00:10:18,873
Wind blast board!

152
00:10:27,433 --> 00:10:28,713
Okay, Sensei.

153
00:10:29,793 --> 00:10:30,623
Godspeed.

154
00:10:52,333 --> 00:10:57,810
Is that the same Elder Dragon who
just several hundred years ago To...

155
00:10:57,893 --> 00:10:59,553
burn down the realm?

156
00:11:07,873 --> 00:11:10,814
It's not going to give me
the chance to retaliate.

157
00:11:12,973 --> 00:11:15,444
Well, I must do something kingly at least.

158
00:11:15,653 --> 00:11:16,993
A grand finale.

159
00:11:18,353 --> 00:11:19,183
Come!

160
00:11:19,413 --> 00:11:20,893
Come get me!

161
00:11:21,913 --> 00:11:25,113
Allow me to show you how resolute we are!

162
00:11:27,693 --> 00:11:29,113
The Blasting Sword.

163
00:11:29,633 --> 00:11:33,973
It channels all the wielder's
sacrificial mana into one final blow.

164
00:11:36,713 --> 00:11:39,073
So he's sacrificing himself.

165
00:11:49,493 --> 00:11:50,773
Do it!

166
00:12:23,013 --> 00:12:24,413
Why?

167
00:12:24,933 --> 00:12:29,133
Why am I, the Elder Dragon,

168
00:12:29,473 --> 00:12:32,133
covered in a cloud of dust?

169
00:12:33,413 --> 00:12:35,813
Because of this little person?

170
00:12:36,273 --> 00:12:42,753
The strong control the weak,
and crush them with violence.

171
00:12:43,533 --> 00:12:47,390
That is the natural law of this world,

172
00:12:47,473 --> 00:12:52,570
and any who dare oppose it shall fall!

173
00:12:52,653 --> 00:12:58,393
Oh, that's what I'm going to do!

174
00:13:02,933 --> 00:13:05,533
Oh, that's what I'm going to do!

175
00:13:06,173 --> 00:13:07,003
Harry!

176
00:13:10,653 --> 00:13:11,993
Ah!

177
00:13:21,653 --> 00:13:23,693
I thought I was just about to die.

178
00:13:25,953 --> 00:13:27,293
Six-Bull Cast!

179
00:13:27,613 --> 00:13:29,073
Wind Blast Force!

180
00:13:44,833 --> 00:13:46,068
Physical enhancement!

181
00:13:48,573 --> 00:13:50,133
Man, that was a close one.

182
00:13:53,093 --> 00:13:54,553
Oh, crap, the walls!

183
00:14:06,033 --> 00:14:07,153
Oh, the dragon!

184
00:14:08,353 --> 00:14:10,693
It was so far away just a second ago.

185
00:14:11,513 --> 00:14:12,413
Oh, God!

186
00:14:12,633 --> 00:14:13,809
I can't stop myself!

187
00:14:13,953 --> 00:14:15,365
I'm gonna smash into it!

188
00:14:18,853 --> 00:14:19,683
Parry!

189
00:14:22,773 --> 00:14:24,733
Well, I made it in one piece.

190
00:14:25,853 --> 00:14:28,912
But I'm gonna tell Lin we're
never doing that again.

191
00:14:31,893 --> 00:14:34,873
Anyways, that was easier
to parry than I expected.

192
00:14:36,133 --> 00:14:39,053
It's a shock how huge
this dragon actually is.

193
00:14:39,813 --> 00:14:42,690
The impact from Lin's magic
really threw me for a loop.

194
00:14:42,773 --> 00:14:46,473
So really, this doesn't
seem all that scary.

195
00:14:47,493 --> 00:14:53,233
Right now, I think I might
be able to fight this thing.

196
00:14:59,533 --> 00:15:02,453
I can't believe all the damage. Right?

197
00:15:03,093 --> 00:15:03,923
Okay then,

198
00:15:04,233 --> 00:15:06,970
the two of us will find the
king and get him out of here,

199
00:15:07,053 --> 00:15:08,970
while Sir Noor fights the Elder Dragon.

200
00:15:09,053 --> 00:15:10,373
Watch out, above you!

201
00:15:26,673 --> 00:15:27,633
Lady Lindbergh!

202
00:15:28,993 --> 00:15:29,823
Thank you.

203
00:15:29,913 --> 00:15:31,230
You just saved my life.

204
00:15:31,313 --> 00:15:34,078
Lady Lindbergh, I need
you to stay close to me.

205
00:15:37,933 --> 00:15:38,763
Goblin!

206
00:15:38,846 --> 00:15:39,676
Emperors!

207
00:15:41,013 --> 00:15:45,013
Comparatively, they're quite small
to the one Noor and I confronted.

208
00:15:45,273 --> 00:15:50,413
But they're still Goblin Emperors, and
they are monsters in a league of their own.

209
00:15:50,933 --> 00:15:52,404
How should we fight them?

210
00:15:52,833 --> 00:15:55,830
I need to start thinking
like Instructor Noor does.

211
00:15:55,913 --> 00:15:56,972
What would he say?

212
00:15:59,073 --> 00:15:59,993
Listen to me.

213
00:16:00,633 --> 00:16:02,515
There's nothing to be afraid of.

214
00:16:03,353 --> 00:16:06,153
Our fight is with some mere Goblins.

215
00:16:09,053 --> 00:16:10,112
Yes, you're right.

216
00:16:10,633 --> 00:16:14,398
Compared to that dragon, this is
something we can easily handle.

217
00:16:15,113 --> 00:16:17,584
Let's keep our cool and take care of this.

218
00:16:20,673 --> 00:16:22,453
Now, ice dance!

219
00:16:28,053 --> 00:16:28,883
Fast!

220
00:16:29,573 --> 00:16:32,393
They still stand down.

221
00:16:32,713 --> 00:16:33,653
Don't move.

222
00:16:36,993 --> 00:16:39,373
I stopped moving!

223
00:16:40,213 --> 00:16:42,273
How he does!

224
00:16:47,633 --> 00:16:49,673
Divine sword!

225
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:05,793
That's a nest for you.

226
00:17:06,213 --> 00:17:09,073
Not only do people call
her the Divine Shield,

227
00:17:09,333 --> 00:17:13,153
but she's more than worthy of
her Divine Sword, Title II.

228
00:17:13,593 --> 00:17:15,190
And while Rolo...

229
00:17:15,273 --> 00:17:19,073
I saw him stop those huge
goblins with just a few words.

230
00:17:19,853 --> 00:17:21,265
Demon folk are a marvel.

231
00:17:21,653 --> 00:17:23,893
So much power within such a young boy.

232
00:17:24,453 --> 00:17:28,335
It must take a great deal of courage
to wield something like that.

233
00:17:30,853 --> 00:17:31,993
Let's get moving!

234
00:17:34,153 --> 00:17:36,513
This makes no sense.

235
00:17:36,733 --> 00:17:38,533
This makes no sense.

236
00:17:38,953 --> 00:17:40,353
This makes no sense.

237
00:17:42,293 --> 00:17:43,453
Harry!

238
00:17:47,033 --> 00:17:48,950
I don't understand.

239
00:17:49,033 --> 00:17:54,050
My claws and scales are indestructible.

240
00:17:54,133 --> 00:17:56,633
How is this happening?

241
00:17:59,613 --> 00:18:04,573
I swear this thing never gets a single
scratch, no matter what hits it.

242
00:18:05,213 --> 00:18:07,801
Seriously, what is the
deal with this sword?

243
00:18:08,313 --> 00:18:10,573
Either way, it is the key to victory.

244
00:18:10,933 --> 00:18:12,953
I might finish this.

245
00:18:13,413 --> 00:18:15,513
I'll use my attack.

246
00:18:15,893 --> 00:18:19,073
That has never failed me.

247
00:18:42,153 --> 00:18:43,553
Harry!

248
00:18:44,513 --> 00:18:45,913
Harry!

249
00:19:04,853 --> 00:19:07,293
He just parried the dragon's breath.

250
00:19:07,913 --> 00:19:08,753
Instructor!

251
00:19:17,633 --> 00:19:19,413
It's angry. Huh?

252
00:19:20,013 --> 00:19:21,913
But it's more than that.

253
00:19:22,873 --> 00:19:27,190
The dragon's frustrated because Noor
isn't treating it as a serious threat.

254
00:19:27,273 --> 00:19:29,508
It's not used to being so disregarded.

255
00:19:31,953 --> 00:19:33,933
Dragons are very prideful beasts.

256
00:19:35,093 --> 00:19:39,681
Especially the Elder Dragon, which
believes it is more powerful than anything.

257
00:19:41,093 --> 00:19:44,973
But in watching this fight,
it's almost as though...

258
00:19:50,453 --> 00:19:53,450
The one who is weak.

259
00:19:53,533 --> 00:19:56,950
The one who is small.

260
00:19:57,033 --> 00:20:00,953
This time is me.

261
00:20:03,733 --> 00:20:04,973
Mary.

262
